  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the sequence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>30</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></msup><mfenced><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>31</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>61</mn></mmultiscripts></mfenced></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
